Start a session from the New session screen without a message.

Start session was disabled until the composer had text or a file, so getting
a sandbox up, for example to use @ file search in its repository, meant
sending a throwaway message. An empty composer now starts the session too,
from the button or Enter. The create was always separate from the first
message: POST /v1/sessions starts the sandbox, and the message follows as an
event. With nothing to send, beginLocalConversation adds no optimistic bubble
and leaves the conversation idle instead of "streaming", and
hydrateLocalConversation binds the session's stream instead of posting a
message. The empty chat then shows the startup card while the sandbox starts,
and "What should we work on?" once it's up. The sidebar row is named after
the agent, such as "Claude Code", as for any untitled session.

Smart Routing is allowed too: the server skips routing on a blank message
and keeps the default harness.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0021-startup-progress.patch.
